Quoting  Doug Freyburger  <dfreybur@yahoo.com>:
>You have not been paying attention to which victims are peaceful and
>which are hostile during your sacrifest.  Here's the relevant lines from
>mon.c on what happens when you kill a monster:
>	} else if (mtmp->mpeaceful)
>		adjalign(-5);
>Killing a peaceful costs 5 points of numerical alignment.

This is not relevant. That checks if the monster is peaceful at the time
of its death. Unless you arrange to kill it in one of a few highly
specific fashions, it isn't; attacking it made it angry. No, one-hit kills
aren't any different. This is a hardy perennial covered at Eva's Myths and
Facts page: http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/index.html#peaceful

>Killing peacefulls is worse:
